WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Since 2024 the London Overground is no longer «the orange line»: it has six lines, each with its own name and colour. Lioness: Euston – Watford Junction. Mildmay: Stratford – Richmond / Clapham Junction. Windrush: Highbury & Islington – Clapham Junction, New Cross, Crystal Palace and West Croydon.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:25.100
Weaver: Liverpool Street – Cheshunt, Enfield Town and Chingford. Suffragette: Gospel Oak – Barking Riverside. Liberty: Romford – Upminster.

3
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:38.100
The signs show the name of the line and the final destination. If you are unsure, ask the staff: in English it is normal to start with «Excuse me».

4
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:54.100
«Mind the gap»: be careful of the gap between the train and the platform. «This train terminates here. All change, please»: the train ends here; everyone gets off. «There are severe delays on the Mildmay line»: there are serious delays on the Mildmay line.

5
00:00:54.100 --> 00:01:01.300
Now do the lesson exercises. If you are unsure, watch this video again.
